Ladybird checks a WebGL vertex attribute offset in the order the spec
gives: negative first, as INVALID_VALUE, then non-zero with no buffer
bound, as INVALID_OPERATION. Chrome 158, Firefox 151, and WebKit 26.5
all do the same, for vertexAttribPointer() and vertexAttribIPointer()
alike, and the test’s output matches each of them line for line.
